a; one of the Pleiades."}]},{"n":"4","spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"N. of the daughter of प्राचेतसदक्ष, one of the 10 wives of Dharma.\n [In mythology Arundhatī is represented as the wife of the sage Vasiṣṭha,\n one of the 7 sages. She was one of the 9 daughters of Kardama Prajāpati\n by Devahūti. She is regarded as the highest pattern of conjugal excellence\n and wifely devotion and is so invoked by the bridegroom at nuptial ceremonies.\n Though a woman she was regarded with the same, even more, veneration as\n the Saptarṣis; cf. "},{"t":"cite","s":"Ku. 6. 12","q":"Ku"},{"t":"txt","s":"; तामगौरवभेदेन मुनींश्चापश्यदीश्वरः ।\n स्त्री पुमानित्यनास्थैषा वृत्तं हि महितं सताम् ॥ cf. also Janakaʼs\n remarks in "},{"t":"cite","s":"U. 4. 10","q":"U"},{"t":"txt","s":". She, like her husband, was the guide and controller\n of Raghuʼs line in her own department and acted as guardian angel to Sītā^1\n after she had been abandoned by Rāma. It is said that Arundhatī (the\n star) is not seen by persons whose end has approached. cf. Suśr. न\n पश्यति सनक्षत्रां यस्तु देवीमरुन्धतीम् । ध्रुवमाकाशगङ्गां च तं वदन्ति\n गतायुषम् ॥; see "},{"t":"cite","s":"H. 1. 66","q":"H"},{"t":"txt","s":" also]."}]},{"n":"5","spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"The tongue (personified).\n.━{@Comp.@}: अरुन्धतीजानिः, अरुन्धतीनाथः, अरुन्धतीपतिः\n[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20251204. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101. note: cf. ap90."}]}],"etym":[{"t":"txt","s":"[न रुन्धती प्रतिरोधकारिणी]"}],"spans":[]}]}],"arunDatijaniH":[{"id":"arunDatIjAniH","headword":"अरुन्धतीजानिः","headword_slp1":"arunDatIjAniH","senses_r":[{"n":1,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"+ -जानिः, -नाथः, -पतिः N. of Vasiṣṭha one of the seven Ṛṣis\n or stars in the Ursa Major. -दर्शनन्यायः see under न्याय."}]}]}],"arunDatinaTaH":[{"id":"arunDatInATaH","headword":"अरुन्धतीनाथः","headword_slp1":"arunDatInATaH","senses_r":[{"n":1,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"+ -जानिः, -नाथः, -पतिः N. of Vasiṣṭha one of the seven Ṛṣis\n 